<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mare Nostrum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mare Nostrum, meaning 'our sea', was the Roman name for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean Sea</a>. It expressed the fact that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> controlled all the lands around it after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and the Hellenistic kingdoms. Roman naval dominance kept the sea secure for trade and the movement of troops across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p></div>
